    "body": "<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nDone.\n\n- **Conflict**: only `.gitkeep` conflicted (auto-generated timestamp lines). Merged `origin/main` (958e410) taking the union of both sides in chronological order — commit 6a7c8e6.\n- **CI fallout from the merge**: `tests/release_workflow_test.rs` then failed on all three platforms (and Test Coverage) for two assertions that my PR's workflow changes invalidated:\n```text\n  - checksum digests are now produced from inside `dist/` (flat names), so `shasum -a 256 dist/*.tar.gz dist/*.cdx.json` no longer appears — updated to assert the flat form, plus a new assertion that the `sha256sum` branch also digests flat names.\n  - the new `verify-published-release-provenance` job adds a third GHCR/Docker Hub login pair, so the exact-count assertions (`DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` 2→3, `username: konard` 2→3, `docker/login-action@` 4→6) were updated with messages naming the provenance job. Commit 8e2a75d.\n- **Verified**: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features`, `rust-script scripts/check-release-workflow.rs`, `check-file-size.rs`, 13/13 `check-release-provenance.rs` unit tests locally; all 29 `release_workflow_test` tests pass.\n- **CI on the branch**: all checks pass (run 31972413415) — Test on ubuntu/macOS/windows, Test Coverage, Lint, Dependency Audit, Build Package, Changelog, Version Modification, Tunnel smoke.\n- PR is now `MERGEABLE`/`CLEAN` and marked ready for review: https://github.com/link-assistant/router/pull/201\n```\n\nWorking tree is clean.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*",
